  "openQuestions": [
    "Image source: both Figma instances are grey #D9D9D9 placeholders with no image fills and figma/assets.json has no entry for either section. Who supplies the photos (collaborator UGC / Instagram embed for guidelines, location photos for neighborhood), and should the guidelines list become a CMS collection list instead of static slot items?",
    "Brief says base text is left-aligned, but the guidelines spec has the heading textAlignHorizontal CENTER and centred on the frame. The plan centres the base heading; confirm.",
    "Scroll reveal: no animation notes exist for either section. Add the global .fade-in / .slide-in reveal to items, or leave static?",
    "#D9D9D9 placeholder fill on the image wrap has no variable. Keep it as a raw placeholder until photos land, or drop the fill once real images exist?"
  ],
  "deviations": [
    "Edge gutter: padding-global is 2rem; Figma items touch 40px (2.5rem) from the 1600 frame edge. Horizontal offsets and widths are percentages of the list width, so they scale with the viewport.",
    "Base vertical overlap uses one is-lift value (-16% of list width). Figma lifts item 2 by about 271px and item 4 by about 221px at 1600 (17.8% and 14.5%); each lands about 25px off.",
    "is-tall uses one 3.125rem gap between items; Figma has 50px, 50px and 117px. The 117px gap before the last item is treated as drift.",
    "Vertical padding: padding-section-large (7rem) top and bottom; the crops show about 115px top and 99px bottom on guidelines and 133px top and 90px bottom on neighborhood.",
    "Mobile (767 and below) is not in Figma. Items keep their alternate offsets at reduced widths (70%, 85% or 100%), lifts reset to 0 and the base heading drops into flow above the list."
  ],
  "buildNotes": [
    "Webflow combo chains: create each item modifier on a scratch element holding only timeline-scatter-images_item plus that one modifier (and likewise for image-wrap), then stack them on the real items. Styling a three-class chain directly creates a selector that only matches that exact chain.",
    "The is-tall modifier goes on the section, header, heading, list and every caption of that instance; the section carries no styles itself.",
    "Set the item tag to figure and the caption tag to figcaption in the Designer; element_builder creates DivBlocks.",
    "No runtime module data attributes: none of A01 to A05 fits a static scattered or zig-zag gallery."
  ],
